      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we must first determine the weight of one canoe and then use that information to find the weight of one bowling ball.\n\nGiven that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds, we can begin by determining the weight of one canoe by dividing 56 by 2. So, one canoe weighs 56 / 2 = 28 pounds.\n\nSince seven identical bowling balls weigh the same as three identical canoes, we know that the weight of seven bowling balls is the same as three canoes. Therefore, if we multiply the weight of one canoe (28 pounds) by 3, we can determine the weight of the seven bowling balls. \n\nSo, the weight of the seven bowling balls is 3 * 28 = 84 pounds.\n\nTo find the weight of one bowling ball, we must divide the weight of the seven bowling balls (84 pounds) by seven. So, one bowling ball weighs 84 / 7 = 12 pounds.\n\nIn conclusion, one of the identical bowling balls weighs 12 pounds.",
